dsv41 patch 0047 v2 (19./20.10.2026): adaptive verify window with two regimes. The scheduler sets the next step's
draft count from the requests' recent acceptance, within the dynamic speculation schedule (0040).
Base: vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py incl. our 0031c; vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py as in the image.
Why: at one stream a narrower window (k = 4 / 3 / 2 instead of 5) decoded prose +1.3 / +4.0 / +5.7 % faster at T = 0
(+1.1 / +4.3 / +5.1 % at T = 1) with the same 2.0 tokens per round, i.e. the unused window rows cost ~5 %; code lost
3 / 7 / 18 % and JSON 6 / 9 / 19 %, they need the depth.
How: with a dynamic speculation schedule, k = min(schedule[n], max over the step's decode requests of
ceil(EMA(accepted drafts) + margin)), at least K_MIN; a request without history (new, or in a prefill chunk) asks for
the full schedule. A round that accepted every draft of its window counts one extra (it might have taken more).
Two regimes (v2): a request whose EMA is at least AK_HI (code, JSON: ~3 accepted drafts a round, in bursts) keeps the
full schedule; below it (prose: ~1) the window follows the EMA. Only for steps with at most MAX_REQS requests; CUDA
graphs for the extra widths are captured for those batch sizes only (cudagraph_utils.py). The verify step itself is
unchanged: as with the stock schedule, only the number of drafts varies.
Measured (GB10, 2000 MHz, decode tok/s against the same setup without the switch; logic tests 9/9 and 7/7):
- one regime (v1), margin 1.0: prose 1 stream T = 0 +7.7 %, 2 streams +10.4 %, 4 streams (MAX_REQS 4) +6.0 %, but code
  T = 0 -3.8 % and JSON T = 1 -10.6 %: after a few weak rounds the window shrank for requests that need the depth.
- AK_HI 2.0, margin 1.0, up to 2 requests: prose 1 stream T = 0 +7.6 % (38.49 -> 36.74 ms per round), 2 streams
  +10.4 %, code and JSON T = 0 +-0.2 %, but JSON at T = 1 dropped from 3.98 to 3.49 tokens per round (its EMA falls
  below 2.0 at T = 1).
- AK_HI 1.6, margin 1.0, up to 4 requests, on top of 0042b's ring kernel from 9 rows, against the production without
  both (ring alone in brackets): prose 1 stream T = 0 +5.1 % (-0.2), prose 3 / 4 streams -0.3 / +9.3 % (+1.6 / +6.6),
  JSON T = 1 1 stream 4.05 against 4.11 tokens per round, JSON 3 / 4 streams +3.4 / +3.3 % (+5.1 / +3.4), code 3 / 4
  streams +3.7 / +5.0 % (+5.0 / +7.7), geometric mean +2.01 % (+2.35 %). So it helps prose at 1 and 4 streams and
  costs code and JSON at 3-4 streams 1-3 % in this run; we run it for the single-stream prose case.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_ADAPTIVE_K=1 (default 0 = off), VLLM_DSV41_AK_MARGIN (default 1.5; we use 1.0), VLLM_DSV41_AK_HI
(default 99 = one regime; we use 1.6), VLLM_DSV41_AK_MAX_REQS (default 2; we use 4), VLLM_DSV41_AK_MIN (2),
VLLM_DSV41_AK_ALPHA (weight of the newest round in the EMA, 0.3). Needs num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size in the
speculative config; without it nothing changes.

